      - Fix: -id:add_usi now populates the USI column for idXML/consensusXML by resolving the MS run from
        the run's spectra_data via the merge index, instead of the never-populated per-ID base_name
        (#9657, fixes #8470)
    IDMerger:
      - Fix: merged output preserves input file order; IdentificationRuns were previously sorted
        alphabetically by run identifier (#9240)
    MSstatsConverter:
      - Added -remove_shared_peptides (default true) to explicitly control whether shared peptides are
        removed; this filtering was previously silent and hardcoded, and a warning now reports how many
        hits were dropped (#9068)
      - MSstatsConverter and ProteomicsLFQ -out_msstats now warn when one MSstats_BioReplicate value
        occurs under more than one MSstats_Condition. That encodes a paired / repeated-measures
        design, which MSstats models differently from an unpaired one; sdrf-pipelines assigns a
        globally unique id per source name, so a recurrence usually means a hand-written design. It
        is a legitimate encoding when intended, so this warns rather than refuses (#9864)
    Epifany:
      - Fix: -exp_design was documented as "(Currently unused)" but has always been used. On
        consensusXML input it merges protein identifications across the fractions and replicates of
        each sample; without it every ID run is merged into one. The description now says so, and
        notes that the parameter is ignored for idXML input (#9864)
      - Fix: an input file whose type could not be determined crashed the tool (SIGABRT) instead of
        returning an error. fatalErrorIf_ threw an int while main_ catches ExitCodes; exception
        matching does not convert an int to an enum and TOPPBase has no catch-all, so the throw
        escaped main(). It now returns ILLEGAL_PARAMETERS. Present since the tool was merged in
        #3485 (2018); only reachable with an input unidentifiable by both extension and content,
        since a recognized-but-wrong format is rejected before main_ runs (#9901)
    Triqler support removed:
      - BREAKING: Triqler export was removed from OpenMS entirely -- the TriqlerConverter tool, the
        ProteomicsLFQ -out_triqler output, and the TriqlerFile library class and its test.
      - The TriqlerConverter tool had never worked. Since it was introduced in #5066 (2020) it read two
        parameters -- 'method' and 'retention_time_summarization_method' -- that were never registered,
        so every invocation aborted with "Internal error: Request for unregistered parameter 'method'"
        and produced no output. The defect survived because the tool had no test. Neither parameter was
        ever usable (an unregistered parameter never reaches the CLI, INI or CTD) and neither had an
        effect to restore.
      - -out_triqler did work, but had no known consumer: quantms, the main downstream pipeline, does
        not pass it (it requests -out_cxml, -out, -out_qpx and -out_msstats), and no other caller was
        found. It also carried two unresolved defects -- runs were keyed per (file, fraction) rather
        than per sample, so fractions of one sample were split across Triqler runs, and rows differing
        only in search score compared equal and silently collapsed to the first one inserted.
      - Migration: use -out_msstats, or -out_cxml / -out_qpx and convert downstream. Existing INIs and
        command lines passing -out_triqler now fail with an unknown-parameter error rather than
        silently dropping the output (#9898)
    MetaboliteAdductDecharger:
      - Added multimer detection (dimers, trimers, ...) with new max_multimer and multimer_log_penalty
        parameters; features are annotated with [nM+adduct]+ style strings (#8888)
    MetaboliteSpectralMatcher:
      - New ccs_error_percent parameter (default 0 = disabled) filters library candidates by relative CCS
        error; missing observed CCS is non-filtering (Skyline convention). mzTab output gains
        opt_observed_ccs, opt_library_ccs and opt_ccs_error_percent; 1/K0 drift times are converted to
        CCS automatically (#8784, #9412)
    FeatureFindingMetabo, MetaboliteFeatureDeconvolution:
      - New opt-in RT-overlap reference options group low-intensity isotope/adduct traces that are much
        shorter in RT than the dominant trace they belong with: 'isotope_rt_overlap_reference'
        (longer|shorter) and 'min_isotope_rt_overlap' (default 0.7) for FeatureFindingMetabo, with a
        matching option for MetaboliteFeatureDeconvolution (#4483, #9711)
    FeatureFinderIdentification (and the FeatureFinderIdentificationAlgorithm library class):
      - Fix: the run summary reported a garbage count of external peptides ("12 peptides identified
        (12 internal, 140724733953152 additional external)"). n_external_peps_ was assigned only when
        external identifications were supplied, but read unconditionally, so without them statistics_()
        formatted an uninitialised member -- undefined behaviour, and visible in every ProteomicsLFQ
        and FeatureFinderIdentification run that does not use external IDs. Both peptide counters are
        now initialised, and the external one is reset per run rather than only inside that branch, so
        a reused algorithm object cannot carry the previous run's count into the next one
      - BREAKING: removed the "external" peptide ID path, and with it the external peptide counter
        fixed above. The -id_ext input, the SVM feature classifier (all 'svm:*' parameters), the
        SVM-based FDR estimation and 'extract:rt_quantile' are gone, along with the
        FFIDAlgoExternalIDHandler class. No in-tree caller ever passed external IDs (ProteomicsLFQ
        and OpenNuXL always passed empty lists) and the only test exercising the path had been
        disabled for years. FeatureFinderIdentificationAlgorithm::run() now takes (peptides,
        proteins, features, seeds, spectra_file); the 'unknown' feature class, the
        "implied"/"external" FFId_category values and the 'rt_delta', 'predicted_class' and
        'FDR_probabilities' meta values are no longer produced (#9995, #10011)
    FeatureFinderMetaboIdent:
      - Added an optional "Adduct" column to the TSV input; m/z is computed via AdductInfo from any
        supported notation (e.g. [M+Na]+, [M-H]-, [2M+H]+) and features are annotated with the adduct.
        Backward compatible (#9382)
    FeatureFinderCentroided:
      - Reworked the algorithm to omit a RAM-costly copy; RAM usage reduced by around 20% (#9159)
    FeatureFinderAlgorithmPicked:
      - Fix: 'mass_trace:mz_tolerance' and 'isotopic_pattern:mz_tolerance' were swapped in
        updateMembers_(); no effect at the default values (both 0.03), but wrong when tuned
        independently (#9247, #9250)
    FeatureFinderMultiplex, MultiplexResolver:
      - BREAKING: parameter `missed_cleavages` renamed to `max_nr_labelled_aas` (#8911)
    FeatureLinkerUnlabeled, FeatureLinkerUnlabeledQT, FeatureLinkerUnlabeledKD, FeatureLinkerWNet:
      - BREAKING: the -design parameter was removed. Multi-fraction grouping never worked: the loop over
        fractions re-used the first k feature maps for every fraction and each group() call cleared the
        output map, so a design with n fractions silently yielded the grouping of a single fraction and
        dropped the remaining input maps without a warning. FeatureLinkerUnlabeled registered the
        parameter but never read it. Link each fraction separately and combine the results with
        FileMerger -append_method append_cols; fractionated label-free quantification is covered by
        ProteomicsLFQ, which does its own per-fraction linking (#10043)
    IDConflictResolver:
      - Added a rank aggregation resolve method (--resolve_method rank_aggregation) for consensus
        replicate identifications (#8907)
    MaRaClusterAdapter:
      - Consensus spectra are annotated with original native IDs, file origins and cluster size (#8864)
    OpenSwathChromatogramExtractor:
      - Compound identifiers in output chromatograms for metabolite targets use the CompoundName
        user-param instead of the compound id, aligning with OpenSwathWorkflow (#9271)
    MetaProSIP:
      - Added detailed documentation of the CSV output column formats (#4400)
    GenericWrapper:
      - BREAKING: the GenericWrapper tool was removed; migrate to direct TOPP tool invocations or TOPPAS
        workflows. The orphaned share/OpenMS/TOOLS/EXTERNAL .ttd tree and its R helper scripts were
        removed along with it (#8981, #9735)
  New tools:
    - FeatureLinkerWNet: groups corresponding features across label-free maps using Wasserstein (optimal
      transport) distance over (m/z, RT) space, solving a minimum-cost network flow via the wnetalign
      library; supports Da and ppm m/z tolerances, L1/L2/Linf metrics and intensity normalization (#8992)
    - UniPEFF: converts UniProtKB XML databases (.xml/.xml.gz) to PEFF 1.0 with PName/GName/NcbiTaxId/
      TaxName/Length/SV/EV/PE/ID/AltAC metadata, ModRes*, VariantSimple/VariantComplex, Processed and
      (with -AnnotationIdentifiers) DisulfideBond annotations; modification accessions are resolved via
      the bundled UniProt ptmlist.txt, PSI-MOD.obo and an optional unimod.obo (#9649)
    - OpenSwathInfer: peptidoform, peptide, protein and gene inference for OpenSWATH analyses (#9280)
    - OpenSwathExport: exports OpenSwathWorkflow results to TSV/Parquet (#9377)
    - OpenSwathPercolatorScoring: scores OpenSwathWorkflow results with Percolator (#9695)
    - OpenSwathPeakMapExtractor: extracts full peakmap points from mzML via targeted extraction (#9684)
