GUI tools:
  - TOPPView and TOPPAS now forward generic Qt command line options (-style, -stylesheet, -platform, ...)
    to Qt instead of aborting with "Unknown option(s)" (fixes #4963)
  - TOPPView: each MS2 precursor's isolation window is drawn as a dashed line in the 2D view; precursor
    markers are selectable and display RT, m/z and charge (#9715)
  - Fix: TOPPAS no longer crashes on shutdown (partial teardown fired signals to already-destroyed
    subcomponents); DataValue-to-string conversions in TOPPView no longer throw for non-string values (a
    regression from the String -> std::string migration); Windows 11 spinbox layouts are no longer too
    narrow; the GUI was converted to the compile-time-checked Qt::connect syntax and gained a
    dismissable splash screen (#9723)
  - Fix: TOPPView no longer segfaults on extreme zoom in the 1D view in SNAP intensity mode, where an
    empty visible m/z range collapsed the intensity range to [0, 0] (#9206, #9263)
  - Fix: TOPPView performance regression when right-clicking in large mzML files (#8997)
  - Fix: Annotation1DItem was missing the OPENMS_GUI_DLLAPI export macro, so its symbols and vtable were
    not exported on Windows DLL builds (#9831)
  - Fix: TOPPView's identification view appended PeakAnnotation::charge to fragment ion labels that
    already spelled the charge out, so every singly charged ion of e.g. an OpenNuXL, SimpleSearchEngine
    or ProSE result was drawn as "y1++", i.e. doubly charged (#8766)
  - Fix: viewing a spectrum in TOPPView rewrote the stored fragment annotations. The identification view
    put the charge into the peak label, and the annotations are synchronised back into the PeptideHit on
    every spectrum switch, so simply stepping through spectra turned NucleicAcidSearchEngine's "a2-B"
    into "a2-B-" and OpenPepXL's "[alpha|ci$y3]" into "[alpha|ci$y3]++" -- which in turn made the
    sequence diagram file an a-B ion under "a". The charge now travels on the annotation item and is
    drawn from there, so the ion name a producer wrote is never modified by looking at it
  - Fix: reading a peak label back cut the charge off the ion name while the identification view put it
    back on the next redraw, so a round trip turned "y3+" into "y3++"
  - Fix: TOPPView kept only the first extra line of a multi-line peak label and dropped blank lines, so
    a comment under the ion name was silently truncated on every spectrum switch
  - Fix: TOPPView derived the fragment ordinal for its sequence annotation by deleting the characters
    that are not the ordinal, so a loss ion like "y3-H2O1+" yielded ordinal 0 and no sequence at all;
    the ordinal is now read as the digits following the ion letter and range-checked against the peptide
  - Fix: TOPPView's sequence diagram for a b ion collapsed everything between the first and last
    modification into a single "*", dropping the residues in between (a doubly modified prefix such as
    "PEPT(Phospho)IDM(Oxidation)" was drawn as "PEPT*" instead of "PEPT*IDM*")
  - TOPPView no longer draws an explicit "1+"/"1-" on singly charged fragments whose name leaves the
    charge to PeakAnnotation::charge (cross-link, NucleicAcidSearchEngine and OpenNuXL ions); charge 1
    is implied, matching how a named "y3+" is already drawn without its sign

OpenMS Library:
  Added:
    - BrukerTimsFile: reader for the Bruker TimsTOF .d directory format (BRUKER_TDF); supports DDA-PASEF,
      DIA-PASEF and raw frame-level 4D access, requires WITH_TIMSRUST=ON (#8975). Further work:
      - tiered scan -> 1/K0 calibration with three fallback levels (Bruker SDK -> rational function from
        the TimsCalibration table -> linear), with the new RationalScan2ImConverter (#8999)
      - MS1 frame aggregation for DIA/DDA-PASEF: ms1_n_neighbors, ms1_min_support,
        ms1_max_rt_distance_sec and ms1_centroid_max_peaks sum peaks from 2N+1 adjacent MS1 frames into
        a sparse (mz_bin, scan_id) grid, composable with the within-frame IM centroiding. Disabled by
        default and exposed via FileConverter -bruker:* (#9151)
      - IM-axis hill centroiding via the new PASEFHillCentroider (hill detection with valley splitting,
        configurable m/z linking tolerance and scan gap), applied to MS1 and DIA/DDA MS2 (#9380)
      - Config fields frame_id_min/frame_id_max and rt_min_sec/rt_max_sec for raw frame-ID and RT range
        filtering; memory and I/O now scale with the requested range, not the file size (#9387)
      - Perf: FrameAggregator switched to boost::unordered_flat_map; 2.1x-3.2x faster finalize per call,
        ~18% end-to-end wall-time reduction on DIA-PASEF files (#9243)
      - DDA MS2 native IDs changed from "scan=<precursor_id>" to
        "frame=<frame_id> scan=<scan_begin> precursor=<precursor_id>", following the PSI-MS MS:1002818
        convention; the precursor token is required for uniqueness under PASEF co-isolation
      - DDA-PASEF and DIA-PASEF spectra are marked as CENTROID so downstream tools accept them without
        an extra conversion (#9154); fixed an off-by-one in the MS1 centroid cap (#9233)
    - ThermoRawFile: native reading of Thermo .raw into MSExperiment via the openms-thermo-bridge (.NET
      managed DLL bridge, fetched via FetchContent, WITH_THERMO_RAW ON by default except on
      Linux/aarch64). Extracts full mzML-equivalent metadata -- per-spectrum TIC, base peak m/z and
      intensity, lowest/highest observed m/z, scan filter string, scan window, ion injection time,
      polarity, and instrument source/analyzer/detector info -- so output matches msconvert/ProteoWizard
      (#9389, #9623)
    - IMAGING module for imaging mass spectrometry: IonImage (dense WxHxD intensity grid with per-pixel
      validity mask and m/z extraction window), MSImagingGeometry (pixel list with (x,y,z) -> spectrum
      index lookup and pixel-size metadata) and MSImagingExperiment (pixel-based spectrum access and
      ion-image extraction); pyOpenMS bindings included (#9381). Further work:
      - ImzMLFile for imzML: in-memory and on-disc (OnDiscImzMLExperiment) loading, streaming via
        IMSDataConsumer, geometry-driven store() with external .ibd arrays at configurable
        float32/float64 precision, and FileTypes::IMZML detection (#9383)
      - BrukerTimsImagingFile for Bruker .d MALDI imaging: reads pixel layout from MaldiApplicationInfo
        and maps each spot to an (x, y) coordinate; CENTROID and PROFILE export modes, WITH_OPENTIMS
        (#9383)
      - multi-region support via the new MSImagingRegion class (axis-aligned rectangle or bbox-local
        bitmask footprint in global pixel coordinates) and a region overlay on MSImagingGeometry
        (addRegion/removeRegion/regionOf/getRegionPixels/getRegionSpectrumIndices); regions form a
        disjoint partition with membership derived on demand. MSImagingExperiment gains a per-region
        extractIonImage(mz, tolerance_ppm, region_id) overload (#9521)
      - on-disc ion image extraction: the shared kernel in IonImageExtraction.h is used by both the
        in-memory and the on-disc path, so single-mass ion images can be visualized from large imzML
        datasets without a full load (one fseek+fread per pixel) (#9654)
      - per-peak auxiliary FloatDataArrays (e.g. ion mobility, MS:1003006) are now read/written as
        external .ibd arrays for both in-memory and on-disc loads, instead of being dropped on write and
        never filled on read; getIMPeakType() is set to IM_PROFILE and getIMUnit() resolves the unit from
        the PSI-MS ontology (1/K0 for MS:1003006, not milliseconds). OnDiscImzMLExperiment now also
        rejects zlib-compressed m/z/intensity arrays like the in-memory loader (#9908)
      - imzML export warns about per-peak Integer/StringDataArrays (e.g. a "charge array" carried over
        from mzML): the format stores only FloatDataArrays, so they were silently dropped before
        (#10002)
    - Native Parquet I/O for identifications, features and consensus maps:
      - PSMArrowIO reads/writes the .idparquet directory bundle (psms/proteins/protein_groups/
        search_params.parquet), lossless round-trip from PeptideIdentificationList and
        ProteinIdentification; QPXFile::importFromArrow() converts a PSMSchema Arrow table directly to a
        PeptideIdentificationList (#9225, #9232)
      - FeatureMapArrowIO and ConsensusMapArrowIO back the .featureparquet and .consensusparquet bundles;
        new FileTypes::IDPARQUET, FEATUREPARQUET and CONSENSUSPARQUET enum values, with
        FileTypes::isDirectoryType() returning true for them and for BRUKER_TDF (#9225, #9242)
      - ArrowSchemaRegistry centralizes all Arrow/Parquet schema definitions with strict (write) and
        subset (read) validation modes (#8970)
      - ArrowExport helper for exporting MSExperiment to Arrow/Parquet with configurable layouts and
        compression (#8655); ProteinGroupArrowExport for the QPX pg schema (#8973)
      - Fix: FeatureMap-level MetaValues (e.g. the spectra_data value set by setPrimaryMSRunPath) are
        preserved across .featureparquet store/load via a new fmap_metavalues key, mirroring the existing
        cmap_metavalues handling; previously they were dropped, propagating filename='UNKNOWN' downstream
        (#9242)
      - Fix: Parquet load synthesizes fresh ProteinIdentification run identifiers, mirroring IdXMLFile,
        and the store side rejects duplicate identifiers before any Arrow builder is allocated (#9242)
    - Percolator: in-process semi-supervised target/decoy rescoring engine based on a vendored subset of
      Percolator 3.08 (with TRON solver); rescore() for combined train+score, train()+score() for split
